Source: duckdb-fdw
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~), postgresql-server-dev-all, libduckdb (>= 1.5.5)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/alitrack/duckdb_fdw

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-duckdb-fdw
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-duckdb-fdw
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libduckdb (>= 1.5.5)
Description: DuckDB Foreign data wrapper extension for PostgreSQL PGVERSION
  This is a foreign data wrapper (FDW) to connect PostgreSQL to DuckDB database file.
  This FDW uses DuckDB's native C API for analytical scans, writes, schema import,
  and data-lake access. It is built from the 2.0.1 snapshot at 9354241 against
  the standalone DuckDB 1.5.5 library.
